{"Global color function migration from scale-color to dark-light-choose creates high churn risk of visual regressions and merge conflicts, plus potential compile issues if variables are missing in some themes": 0.054067838937044144, "Widespread changes to high-PR files (admin_base.scss, headers, topic lists, topic posts) amplify risk that a single theming tweak or bug will ripple through large portion of UI": 0.02281096950173378, "In admin_base.scss, h3 color for .setting.overridden uses scale-color($highlight, $lightness: -50%) bypassing dark-light-choose pattern, creating potential contrast issues in dark themes": 0.06620868295431137, "admin_base.scss has multiple scale-color usages not wrapped by dark-light-choose (lines 418, 443, 496), breaking dark-mode support consistency": 0.03540659323334694, "Typo/syntax error in topic-list SCSS patch shows truncated 'color: dark-ligh' which would cause compile-time SCSS error": 0.05017466843128204, "In _topic-list.scss line 115, color uses scale-color($primary, $lightness: 50%) without dark-light-choose wrapper, inconsistent with surrounding usage": 0.08995213359594345, "Header color rule at line 301 uses dark-light-choose with primary as light-theme color, contradicting goal of dark-theme colors relying on $secondary": 0.020742276683449745, "Header color rule at line 332 reuses primary in dark-light-choose call, risking dark-theme deriving from primary rather than secondary": 0.006532648578286171, "Centralized dark-light-choose function creates tight coupling between theming palette and all UI components - changes to primary/secondary colors or brightness logic will cascade across thousands of style rules": 0.004774422384798527, "Large-scale color refactor in desktop topic-list styling may lead to inconsistent theming across breakpoints if secondary color not defined identically in all themes": 0.0031443885527551174, "Mobile topic list styling updates add churn across mobile styles with potential for regressions in mobile rendering": 0.0008759566699154675, "No explicit color-contrast tests or visual regression tests across light and dark themes despite hundreds of components relying on new color logic": 0.0024863346479833126, "Broad patch scope touching desktop, mobile, and admin styles increases surface area for regressions": 0.0010373415425419807, "dark-light-choose function relies on theme_variables imports - if import graph changes or theme_variables unavailable in some build contexts, builds could fail": 0.0006427721818909049, "PR description is minimal ('Test 7') and does not summarize changes, rationale, affected files, or testing performed": 0.07527066767215729, "No CHANGELOG.md present despite project referencing standard changelog practices - change affecting theming/tokens should have changelog entry": 0.004369035363197327, "Partial adoption with some color usages remaining as direct tokens (e.g., color: $primary) creates mixed color strategies within same theme": 0.0026075716596096754, "Static uses of $header_primary in topic-post.scss not part of dark-theme toggle via dark-light-choose, making dark-theme behavior potentially inconsistent": 0.009427775628864765, "No dark-theme-specific tests found in test folder covering dark-theme behavior or fallback logic": 0.001374459476210177, "No visual regression or theming tests that would guard the CSS theming changes introduced by this PR": 0.015361165627837181}